<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korea plans to cut sulphur in products - table.</title>
<headline>South Korea plans to cut sulphur in products - table.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea plans to cut the sulphur content in various oil products in coming years as part of tougher laws on the environment.</p>
<p>The following table provides a summary on the requirements, based on information from the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy.</p>
<p>(The figures show the percentage content of sulphur in the products):</p>
<p>	    DIESEL			   KEROSENE	  FUEL OIL</p>
<p>Current   0.1 (cars)		     0.08		1.0</p>
<p>1997 Jul  0.1 (industrial, home)			   0.5 (urban)</p>
<p>1998 Apr  0.05 (cars)</p>
<p>1999								 0.5 (rural)</p>
<p>Gradual					no target</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom, (+822 727 5643)</p>
</text>
